 <scopecontent id="scopecontent-1.8.3">
 <head>Scope and Content</head>
 <p>Collection contains radio, motion picture, and television scripts written by Mort Fine and David Friedkin. Also contains business records of Friedkin &amp; Fine, including contracts, production reports, story ideas, and business and personal correspondence. Includes scripts for such television programs as the <title linktype="simple">Alfred Hitchcock Hour</title>, <title linktype="simple">I Spy</title>, <title linktype="simple">Our Miss Brooks</title>, and <title linktype="simple">The Virginian</title>. Two phonograph records of radio shows are shelved separately.</p>
 </scopecontent>
 <arrangement id="arrangement-1.8.4">
 <head>Organization and Arrangement</head>
 <p>Arranged in the following series: <list type="ordered"><item>Television plays (Boxes 1-6).</item><item>Radio scripts (Boxes 7-12).</item><item>Motion picture screenplay and musical review (Box 12).</item><item>Business records of Friedkin &amp; Fine (Boxes 13-17).</item><item>Friedkin &amp; Fine personal and miscellaneous (Boxes 17-18).</item></list></p>
 </arrangement>
